scaleplex: vf_inlineass CUDA branch — GPU-resident text/ASS sub-burn (#76, #107)

CUDA hardware branch mirroring the VAAPI branch. libass renders the cue at
render_height into a straight-alpha RGBA buffer; swscale converts it to a
render-dims YUVA420P CUDA overlay surface; a per-plane alpha-blend kernel
(adapted from vf_overlay_cuda.cu, LGPL-2.1) reads the overlay + alpha through
cached CUDA texture objects (normalized coords + hardware bilinear) and blends
onto the CUDA video frame in place. The render->full upscale is folded into the
blend (free HW bilinear), so there is no per-frame CPU swscale upscale (#107);
the texture objects are created once over the stable overlay surface (no
per-frame cuTexObjectCreate). Removes the per-frame full-frame hwdownload the
interim path required (worker subBurnDownloadFilter -> "").

Text/ASS only; bitmap (PGS) on CUDA out of scope. Gated on CONFIG_OVERLAY_CUDA_FILTER.

